      "message": "Hmm, good point...\n\nI think you\u0027re saying that all errors should be moved to the linting layer and so the transformation of AST -\u003e Rust should be a function which cannot fail? That should be the end goal, in my opion.\n\nI introduced many code generating functions which return `Result`, but at least some of them look unnecessary. As an example, we could also crash if this function fails since it would mean that we have an internal error in the compiler:\n\n```rust\nfn type_for_width(width: usize) -\u003e Result\u003csyn::Type\u003e {\n    let rounded_width \u003d round_bit_width(width)?;\n    syn::parse_str(\u0026format!(\"u{rounded_width}\")).map_err(anyhow::Error::from)\n}\n```",
